{% when 'tracekit-intelligence-guide' %}
<div class="tk-guide-hero"><span class="tk-ip-kicker">TRACEKIT INTELLIGENCE</span><h1>From a business question to supporting evidence</h1><p>Investigate business records while keeping source relationships and uncertainty visible.</p><div class="tk-guide-meta"><span>TRACEKIT LEARNING LIBRARY</span><span>6–8 MIN READ</span><span>EDUCATIONAL GUIDE</span></div></div>
<div class="tk-guide-layout"><aside class="tk-guide-sidebar"><strong>IN THIS GUIDE</strong><nav aria-label="Article sections"><a href="#chapter-1">01 / Ask a precise question</a><a href="#chapter-2">02 / Follow the evidence</a><a href="#chapter-3">03 / Show unresolved findings</a><a href="#chapter-4">04 / Respect permissions</a><a href="#chapter-5">05 / Built-in and external Intelligence</a></nav><a href="/pages/resources">← All resources</a></aside><article class="tk-guide-article">
<section id="chapter-1"><span class="tk-guide-index">01 / GUIDE SECTION</span><h2>Ask a precise question</h2><p>Start with a specific business question, such as which affiliates are associated with disputes or why conversions differ from orders. Define the time period and data scope.</p><div class="tk-guide-diagram"><span>ILLUSTRATIVE CONCEPT</span><div class="tk-guide-flow" role="img" aria-label="Question → Source records → Evidence"><div class="tk-guide-flow-step"><small>STEP 01</small><strong>Question</strong></div><span class="tk-guide-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="tk-guide-flow-step"><small>STEP 02</small><strong>Source records</strong></div><span class="tk-guide-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="tk-guide-flow-step"><small>STEP 03</small><strong>Evidence</strong></div></div></div></section>
<section id="chapter-2"><span class="tk-guide-index">02 / GUIDE SECTION</span><h2>Follow the evidence</h2><p>A defensible answer should identify the supporting source records and distinguish commerce identity from attribution identity. Correlation is not proof of causation.</p><div class="tk-guide-insight"><strong>Key point</strong><p>Explain what supports each conclusion.</p></div></section>
<section id="chapter-3"><span class="tk-guide-index">03 / GUIDE SECTION</span><h2>Show unresolved findings</h2><p>Imagine a fictional set of 12 disputes: seven linked to Affiliate A, three to Affiliate B, and two unattributed. The two unresolved cases are part of the answer, not a gap to hide.</p><div class="tk-guide-diagram"><span>ILLUSTRATIVE CONCEPT</span><div class="tk-guide-flow" role="img" aria-label="7 matched + 3 matched + 2 unresolved = 12"><div class="tk-guide-flow-step"><small>STEP 01</small><strong>7 matched + 3 matched + 2 unresolved = 12</strong></div></div></div></section>
<section id="chapter-4"><span class="tk-guide-index">04 / GUIDE SECTION</span><h2>Respect permissions</h2><p>Data visibility and governed actions depend on account, organization, client context, and permissions. The presence of a tool does not grant every user authority to execute it.</p><blockquote>Governed access is part of trust.</blockquote></section>
<section id="chapter-5"><span class="tk-guide-index">05 / GUIDE SECTION</span><h2>Built-in and external Intelligence</h2><p>TraceKit Intelligence is intended for use within the product. Compatible external clients may access supported governed tools via MCP when configured and permitted. Availability depends on production readiness.</p><div class="tk-guide-insight"><strong>Key point</strong><p>MCP is optional, not required.</p></div></section>
